Blocked: a multi-line body may not be passed inline with --comment/-c.

  command: gh pr close -R foo/bar 1 -c $'line1\nline2'

Combining --comment "$(...)" with a heredoc stacks two layers of quoting, and a
mis-escape — a stray backslash before a backtick — ends up in the published
text.

Fix: write the body to a file (a scratchpad, say), post it with
gh pr comment --body-file, and run close without -c:
  gh pr comment -R owner/repo 123 --body-file /path/to/body.md
  gh pr close -R owner/repo 123
